      "writtenOn": "2026-03-24T15:48:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When `prune_single_ref` is 1, 2 (less aggressive) we disallow pruning of certain reference frames at block level (pruned based on temporal distance and `pred_mv_sad[ref_frame]`, in the function `init_mode_skip_mask()`). The flag `cpi-\u003ekeep_single_ref_frame_mask` populated in this function decides which of the reference frames should not be pruned. However, when ‘prune_single_ref’ is 3, 4 (more aggressive) all reference frames are allowed to be pruned at block level and thus the flag `cpi-\u003ekeep_single_ref_frame_mask` is set to 0. We have slightly modified the code for improved readability in patchset 5.",
